  "notes": "Prices in USD per 1M tokens, standard (non-batch) API tier. Tiered-price models record the base (lowest) tier with the higher tier in the model's note field. Retired models excluded; deprecated-but-available models included. Collected Monday 2026-09-14, 7 days after the previous file. Tracked scope follows the set established on 2026-07-16 so week-over-week deltas stay meaningful. The set stays at 47 rows: nothing arrived and nothing left, but one row was replaced in place. DeepSeek retired deepseek-v4-flash (DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731) and now serves that model name from DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash under the new canonical id deepseek-flash, billed at the Flash price; the legacy id is still accepted as an alias. The replacement is cheaper on every axis at off-peak rates: cache-miss input $0.22 to $0.15 (-31.8%), output $0.66 to $0.60 (-9.1%), cache-hit input $0.007 to $0.003 (-57.1%). Because the vendor swapped the model behind a retained name, this row is a substitution rather than a like-for-like price cut, and a per-token series that ignores the version change would read it as a discount on a product that no longer exists. The other 46 rows did not move — a third consecutive week with no price change on the carried set, across all six providers. Two vendor statements dated this week bear on scheduled-expiry claims and are recorded here because both cancel a previously announced change: DeepSeek states it will continue serving deepseek-v4-pro after 2026-09-14 with billing unchanged, and Anthropic states that the Claude Sonnet 5 introductory rate of $2/$10, previously scheduled to rise to $3/$15 on 2026-09-01, is now the standard price and that the increase will not occur.",
